==Battleground==
*7 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*6 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*8 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Malevolent Mohawk Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Le'Behemoth]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 113.33~120 seconds<sup>3,400f~3,600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Fallen Bear]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 73.33~80 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is essentially [[Dark Souls (Insane)|Dark Souls]], but everything has the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait. It has only variants of the enemies seen there, too, except for Cerberus Kids. [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|Anti-Aku Cats]] work really nicely here.

Malevolent Mohawk Cat acts like [[Wicked Cat]] but tougher: lots of knockbacks, a [[Shield]] that regenerates for each knockback, and a decent amount of HP before it gets knocked back. While it is recommended to bring a [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]] ([[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] is probably the most ideal non-[[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha]] option), sometimes you may brute force the Shield due to it only having 48k HP. Either way, with or without the shield, Malevolent Mohawk is immune to most crowd-control effects.

Because of the Fallen Bears leaving highly-damaging [[Surge Attack]]s upon death, it is recommended to have at least one [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-Immune unit]] for whenever a surge hits. [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] and [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] work as meatshields for this reason. While not immune to surges, [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydancer Cat]] can dodge all attacks in this stage.

Expect to push a lot in this stage if your units have high DPS. While that may seem like a good thing, pushing too much will cause your cats to get hit by Le'Behemoth, taking massive damage. You should focus on taking out the Le'Behemoths before they are able to stack up, as once they do, they will push extremely hard. Use [[Long Distance]] units like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] to use Malevolent Mohawk as a stepping stone to snipe the Le'Behemoths.

[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], while a difficult unit to get, works immensely well in this stage, dealing excellent damage, slowing anything not protected by a Shield, and avoiding all Surge damage. However, this comes with the caveat of Malevolent Mohawk's counter surge, so anti-surge units would need to support Uril.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]]: Dodges every enemy here and is very cheap to spam, and has high speed.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]: A shield piercer with high speed, range and attack rate, it can help pierce through every shield in this stage, though do note he has Single Target and no ways of hitting the backline, along with lacking any immunity.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]]: Very bulky and has Surge Immunity, this unit will prove useful to you if you can afford its steep cost.
*[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Good piercing chance and piercing range with Surge Immunity adding insurance that a stack of Barrels won't get wiped out. Do note that it has only 2 knockbacks and a blindspot.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]]: Spammable with VERY high bulk and can straight up tank any Surge from the Aku enemies, though at this point if you were able to beat the [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|stage]] to obtain this unit, you won't have any struggles here.
*[[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]]: Although his range is short, he can be helpful as he has a chance to knockback Aku enemies. Do keep in mind that he will need a stepping stone to hit Fallen Bear and Le'Behemoth, however the presence of Malevolent Mohawk can help him in this case.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]]: LD unit with similar range and pierce to Fiend, however trades knockback for slightly higher standing range along with more DPS if you've unlocked her [[Savage Blow]] [[Talents|talent]]. Housewife can be used to snipe Le'Behemoth and Fallen Bear, using Malevolent Mohawk as a stepping stone.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]]: His Long Distance Shield-Piercing attacks can hit the Fallen Bears and Le'Behemoth, guaranteeing a slow if this happens. These odds are increased in True Form and paired with a nice Knockback. However, he isn't very effective against Malevolent Mohawk since the boss is immune to many debuffs.
*[[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Dancer of Grief]]: Low cooldown with piercing attacks that also pierce shields every attack, with Strengthen to deal even more damage. However, do note her poor survivability and range.
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]]: With a low cooldown, very high damage and Omni-Strikes, Saito will easily tear through every enemy here, to the point where he can even chain Malevolent Mohawk and pin him at the base thanks to his Omni-Strike giving him 400 effective range towards bases. Le'Behemoth does pose an issue to Saito, however.
*[[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Hevijak]]: Outranges every enemy here, can Knockback enemies, pierce shields and Resists any attacks that do come his way. His Knockback doesn't affect Malevolent Mohawk, which can work in your favor, considering the fact that Le'Behemoth and Fallen Bear will be repeatedly targeted by his attacks every time they walk within range.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Akuma Hayabusa]]: Similar to Summoner Satoru but with less effectiveness.
*[[White Knight Cyclops (Uber Rare Cat)|White Knight Cyclops/Demon Knight Kyklops]]: Outranges everything here, pierces Shields 50% of the time, and also occasionally Freezes supports too. In true form, Demon Knight Kyklops swaps the Freezes for Massive Damage, which proves more useful against the Freeze-immune boss of this stage.
*[[Bunny & Canard (Uber Rare Cat)| Malevolent Mad Duck]]: Able to deal a huge amount of burst damage to every enemy here, especially considering the fact that they're all Aku. They also have Surge Immunity, so they can't be taken out that easily.
*[[Agent Staal (Uber Rare Cat)|Edgemaster Staal]]: Not only tanky, but also attacks fast and deals a lot of damage. He can also pierce the shields of many of the backliners in this stage with his Mini-Waves that carry his Shield Piercer.
*[[Amakusa Shiro (Uber Rare Cat)|Amakusa Shiro]]: Though it's generally hard to use him since he has Multi-Hit, Amakusa can take out the Le'Behemoths once their shields are pierced due to their singular knockback. Be careful, as he barely outranges their Omni-Strike.
*[[Vornado (Uber Rare Cat)|Vornado]]: Like Amakusa Shiro, but better in basically every way. He outranges the Le'Behemoths Omni-Strike much better, does more damage, has a faster attack rate, and pierce. Another notable thing is that he can Two-Shot the Fallen Bears when their shield is broken, and lacks the Multi-Hit that makes Amakusa much more difficult to use. Though be wary of his blindspot, since if he is left unprotected, it could lead to him dying despite his massive bulk of health, and his cost shouldn't be belittled either, at 5,550¢. Use him carefully.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]]: Hanayama makes any and all Aku a joke, and Century's End is no exception. His bulk of HP, high damage, and 100% shield pierce guarantees any Aku that faces his wrath is either crippled, or dead. And the only enemy that's surviving is Malevolent Mohawk and Le'Behemoth, as everyone else will be taking 300k damage and dying instantly. At level 50, he does double the damage at 600k, which is enough to kill Malevolent Mohawk in 6 hits! Be wary of his long foreswing though.

